-- title:
--   Unit criterion at an end of the blown-up supersingular chart
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ and a positive integer $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$, and a prime $\ell$ with $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell \mid M'$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic $0$ and $\zeta \in L$ a primitive $q$-th root of unity, and assume (`hι`) that there is a ring homomorphism $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota(\zeta) = \exp(2\pi i/q)$. Let $H_1 \le (\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times$ be (`hH₁`) the intersection of [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH q M'`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22), the kernel of the reduction of units along the divisibility `dvd_sq_mul q M'`, with the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/\ell)^\times$. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L \subseteq L((t))$ which (`hK`) is the $L$-subfield generated by the coefficientwise images under [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) of the $q$-expansion function field [`ModularCurve.xHFunctionField (q ^ 2 * M') H₁`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L79) of level [`CohCarrier.GammaH (q ^ 2 * M') H₁`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L133).
--
--   Let $A$ be a Henselian discrete valuation ring with algebraically closed residue field, which is an $A$-algebra structure on $L$ making $L$ its fraction field, with $q$ in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\zeta$ in the image of $A$, together with an $A$-algebra structure on $K$ compatible with $L$. Let $j \in K$ be nonzero with Laurent series the image of [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) under [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81). Let $\varpi$ generate the maximal ideal of $A$, and let $\varpi_t \in A$ satisfy $\varpi_t^{q^2-1} = q u$ for some unit $u$ (`hϖt`). Write $C :=$ `chartAlgFin A ↥K j` for the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ consisting of the elements integral over $A[j]$, and `jChartFin` for $j$ regarded in $C$.
--
--   Let $y$ be a maximal ideal of $C$ containing $\varpi$ such that (`hss`) for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi : C \to \Omega$ with kernel $y$, the element $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), i.e. every elliptic curve over $\Omega$ with that $j$-invariant has no nonzero point killed by $q$.
--
--   The hypothesis `hArig` (a rigidity statement for the two-chart integral model $X :=$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A ↥K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236), the pushout glueing $\operatorname{Spec} C$ to the chart at $j^{-1}$, summarised here) asserts: for every point $z$ of $X$ at which the germ $\varpi_z$ of $\varpi$ pulled back along `toBase` lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk, and every point $y'$ of $\operatorname{Spec} C$ mapping to $z$ under `ιFin` whose prime satisfies the same supersingularity condition as above, there exist a complete discrete valuation ring $W$, a homomorphism $\sigma : A \to W$ with maximal ideal generated by $\sigma \varpi$, power series $f, u, v \in W[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u, v$ units and $f \equiv X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1$ (the form [`DrinfeldCurve.LocalChart.drinfeldForm q W`](def/DrinfeldCurve_LocalChart.html#L18)) modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$, and a ring isomorphism $e$ from the adic completion of the stalk of $X$ at $z$ onto $S := W[[X_0,X_1]]/(\sigma(\varpi_t^{q+1})v - fu)$, subject to a conjunction of clauses: $e$ carries the image of $a \in A$ to the constant $\sigma a$; level automorphisms $\tau$ of $K$ over $L$ attached to $\gamma^{-1}$ for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ preserve $C$; those $\gamma$ with $\gamma_{11} \equiv 1 \bmod \ell$ induce the identity on $C/y'$; each such $\tau$ fixing $C/y'$ is matched, through $e$ and the germ map at $y'$, by an automorphism $\theta$ of $S$ fixing constants and acting on $X_0, X_1$ modulo degree $2$ by a matrix $M$ with $M \equiv c\gamma$ modulo the maximal ideal of $W$, where $c^{q+1} \equiv 1$, where $c \equiv 1$ whenever $\gamma_{11} \equiv 1 \bmod \ell$, and where $c \not\equiv 1$ whenever $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau \ne \mathrm{id}$; two primes of $S$ containing $\sigma\varpi$ and not containing both $X_0$ and $X_1$, with tangent directions $(a_1 : b_1)$ and $(a_2 : b_2)$ that are not proportional modulo $q$, have distinct contractions to the stalk; for a prime with tangent direction $(1 : 0)$, an element of $C$ lies in the contraction of that prime precisely when all its Laurent coefficients lie in the maximal ideal of $A$; and [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L q`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) lies in $K$ and in $C$, and differs from some $a_0 \in A$ by an element of $y'$ whose image under $e$ is the class of a series $h \in (X_0,X_1)^{e_0}$ with $e_0 \ge 1$ whose $e_0$-th homogeneous part takes unit values at all $(a : b)$ over $W$ with $a$ or $b$ a unit and $a^qb - ab^q$ in the maximal ideal.
--
--   The statement then fixes such data: a point $z$ of $X$ with $\varpi_z$ in the maximal ideal of the stalk, a point $y'$ of $\operatorname{Spec} C$ over $z$ satisfying the supersingularity condition and with $y'$ equal to $y$ (`hy'y`), and a particular presentation $W_1, \sigma_1, f_1, u_1, v_1, e_1$ for which the hypothesis `hW₁` asserts the whole conjunction of clauses just listed, with $S$ built from $W_1$.
--
--   Let $J$ be the ideal of $C$ which (`hJ`) is the infimum, over $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ and level automorphisms $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ preserving $C$, of the pullback along $\tau|_C$ of the contraction, along $e_1$ composed with the completion and germ maps at $y'$, of the ideal of $S$ generated by the classes of $\sigma_1\varpi_t$, $X_0$ and $X_1$. Let $B$ be the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ which (`hB`) is generated over $C$ by the elements $x$ with $x\varpi_t \in J$, i.e. $B = C[J/\varpi_t]$. Let $W$ be a valuation subring of $K$ containing $B$ (`hBW`). The remaining structural hypotheses are: `hR1`, that $C \subseteq B$ and every element of $K$ is a quotient of two elements of $B$ with nonzero denominator; `hR2`, that $B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A$ and $B/\varpi B$ has Krull dimension at most $1$; `hR3` (five clauses), that the elements of $L$ lying in $W$ are exactly those of $A$, that the maximal ideal of $W$ is generated by $\varpi$, that $W$ is a discrete valuation ring, that an element of $C$ lies in $y$ exactly when it lies in the maximal ideal of $W$, and that $W$ is the localisation of $B$ at that maximal ideal; and `hEQ` (five clauses, summarised here), that for every $(\mathbb{F}_{q^2})$-algebra structure on the residue field of $A$ there is a surjection $\rho$ from $B$ onto the Drinfeld coordinate ring [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q (ResidueField A)`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) with kernel the elements of $B$ in the maximal ideal of $W$, compatible with $A \to$ `ResidueField A`, and equivariant for the level automorphisms attached to $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ preserving $W$ via an element $(\mathrm{redQ}\,\gamma, c)$ of [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276) acting through [`DrinfeldCurve.hAction`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L325), with $c \ne 1$ when $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau \ne \mathrm{id}$; that all such level automorphisms preserve $B$; that every prime of $B$ containing $\varpi$ is obtained by transporting the maximal ideal of $W$ by some $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$; that an element of $B$ lying in the maximal ideal of $W$ after all such transports is divisible by $\varpi$; and that a level automorphism preserving $y$ on $C$ preserves $W$.
--
--   Finally, let $O$ be a subring of $K$ for which `hO` provides a nonzero $a \in J$ and a maximal ideal $P$ of $B_a := C[J/a]$ such that $O$ is the localisation of $B_a$ at $P$ inside $K$, every element of $y$ lying in $O$ is a non-unit of $O$, and $B$ is not contained in $O$. Assume further $O \subseteq W$ (`hOW`), that $O$ is local (`hOloc`) and Noetherian (`hOnoe`), and that $C \subseteq O$ (`hCO`). The last hypothesis `hIgStab` asserts that every valuation subring $V$ of $K$ whose intersection with $L$ is $A$, in whose maximal ideal $\varpi$ lies, which contains $C$, and for which some $c \in C$ has $p(c)$ a unit of $V$ for every monic $p \in A[X]$, is preserved by all level automorphisms attached to $\gamma^{-1}$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$, in the sense that $f \in V \iff \tau f \in V$.
--
--   Under these hypotheses the conclusion is the following unit criterion. Let $s \in C$ divide a power of $\varpi$ in $C$, that is, $s t = \varpi^k$ for some $k \in \mathbb{N}$ and some $t \in C$. Let $a \in J$ be nonzero in $K$, let $P$ be a maximal ideal of $B_a = C[J/a]$ such that $O$ is the localisation of $B_a$ at $P$ (an element of $K$ lies in $O$ exactly when it is $g/h$ with $g, h \in B_a$ and $h \notin P$), and let $N \in \mathbb{N}$. Assume that $s\,a^{-N} \in O$; that $s\,a^{-N}$, whenever it lies in $W$, is a unit of $W$; and that for every valuation subring $V$ of $K$ such that the elements of $L$ in $V$ are exactly those of $A$, such that $\varpi$, when it lies in $V$, lies in the maximal ideal of $V$, and such that, if $j \in V$ and $p(j)$ is a unit of $V$ for every monic $p \in A[X]$ and $O \subseteq V$, then $s\,a^{-N}$, whenever it lies in $V$, is a unit of $V$. Then $a^N s^{-1} \in O$.
--
--   This is the unit criterion at an end of the blow-up of the supersingular chart of the integral model: an element $s/a^N$ of the local ring $O = C[J/a]_P$ which is a unit of the exceptional discrete valuation ring $W$ and of every Igusa-type valuation ring containing $O$ has its inverse again in $O$. It is used, in the $\Gamma_1(\ell)$-diamond frame with no lower bound imposed on $q$, by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevelOne.exists_verticalUnit_pow_centre_of_end_blowupChart_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevelOne.exists_verticalUnit_pow_centre_of_end_blowupChart_of_dvd), and its proof invokes the Drinfeld-chart rigidity statement `exists_primes_exceptional_igusa_trichotomy_of_end_blowupChart_linked_of_dvd` together with the criterion [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel.forall_monic_aeval_not_mem_maximalIdeal_of_not_isMaximal_centre`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel.forall_monic_aeval_not_mem_maximalIdeal_of_not_isMaximal_centre) for recognising Igusa-type valuation rings.
